the tps file directly.</div><div><br></div><div>Wu<br></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"auto\" class=\"gmail_attr\">在2021年9月3日星期五 UTC+8 下午4:47:00&lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">ant...@gmail.com</a>&gt; 写道：<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:&quot;trebuchet ms&quot;,sans-serif;color:rgb(11,83,148)\">Wu Jin,</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:&quot;trebuchet ms&quot;,sans-serif;color:rgb(11,83,148)\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:&quot;trebuchet ms&quot;,sans-serif;color:rgb(11,83,148)\">this is not really a geomorph question, but rather a basic R one. Please have a look at the string manipulation functions of R, like substr().</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:&quot;trebuchet ms&quot;,sans-serif;color:rgb(11,83,148)\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:&quot;trebuchet ms&quot;,sans-serif;color:rgb(11,83,148)\">Hope this helps</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:&quot;trebuchet ms&quot;,sans-serif;color:rgb(11,83,148)\">Antigoni</div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Fri, Sep 3, 2021 at 10:42 AM Jin Wu &lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">wuj...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><br><div>Hi, <br></div><div><br></div><div>I am doing analysis of shape of one kind of snail that collected from 11 poplations. I have named the jpg files as ZJTL1.jpg, ZJTL2.jpg, ZJTL3..jpg and so on. I want to trim the left 4 characters as population factor to ANOVA analysis the effect on shape.<br></div><div><br></div><div>Regards</div><div>Wu Jin<br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div>\r\n\r\n<p>