   "subject": "Re: [geomorph-r-package] Is it possible trim the text in the filename as a factor?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Wu Jin,<div>as Antigoni said you can use subst function to extract desired number of characters from a string:</div><div><br></div><div>tpsFilePath &lt;- &quot;xyz&quot; [change xyz with the path of your tps file]</div><div><br></div><div>require (geomorph)</div><div><br></div><div>tpsFile &lt;- <span style=\"font-size:12.6px\">readland.tps (tpsFilePath, specID = &quot;imageID&quot;) </span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:12.6px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:12.6px\">idsAll &lt;- dimnames(tpsFile)[[3]]</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:12.6px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:12.6px\">idsFour &lt;- substr (idsAll, 1, 4) # arguments 1 and 4 define the range of characters to be extracted from the string</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:12.6px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:12.6px\">print (idsFour)</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:12.6px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:12.6px\">Best, </span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:12.6px\">Marko</span></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
